    {
      "id": "s02-carrier",
      "intent": "The carrier equation first makes a dense feature field from the low-resolution image, then partitions that field into tokens without dropping them.",
      "claim": "\\mathbf{F}=\\mathcal{E}(\\mathbf{I}_{\\mathrm{LR}}),\\qquad \\mathbf{X}=\\mathcal{W}(\\mathbf{F})",
      "narration": "The encoder takes the low-resolution image and produces the dense feature field. The symbol F is the carrier that preserves the spatial field for later updates. Window partitioning acts on that carrier, turning it into tokens for the thought process. The equation keeps the carrier in the chain instead of replacing the image with only a compact thought.",
